KAKEPHOOA END-USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA)

This Agreement is governed by the Traditional Chinese version below, which
shall control in the event of any discrepancy. By downloading, installing,
or executing the software accompanying this Agreement (the "Software"),
you agree to be bound by the following terms.

1. Definitions

"Licensor" means the publisher of the Software. "You" or "Licensee" means
the individual or entity installing or running the Software. "Single-User
Edition" means the self-hosted distribution of the Software offered free
of charge under this Agreement.

2. Grant of License

Licensor grants You a non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free
license to install and run the Single-User Edition of the Software,
without restriction as to context of use (personal, household, or
internal business use are all permitted), without expiration, and
without any limitation other than as set forth in this Agreement. You
may install and run the Software only within environments You control,
and only for use by You and by members of Your household or
organization.

3. Restrictions on Redistribution

You may not redistribute the Software (whether as a container image or
as a tarball), in whole or in part, modified or unmodified, to any third
party, whether or not for consideration. All users must obtain the
Software solely through the distribution channels designated by Licensor
(the container registry and the public Releases page maintained by
Licensor). Licensor disclaims all liability for any damage arising from
copies obtained through unauthorized redistribution or from versions
that have been modified by parties other than Licensor.

4. Restrictions on Service Provision

You may not use the Software to provide a hosted, managed, or otherwise
publicly or commercially available service to third parties, whether or
not for consideration. Without limiting the foregoing, You may not
operate a deployment that persons outside Your household or
organization are able to register for or otherwise use. Rights to
operate the Software as a service are available separately; enquiries
may be directed to the address in the Contact clause below.

5. Restrictions on Reverse Engineering

You may not decompile, disassemble, or otherwise reverse engineer the
Software, except to the extent such restriction is expressly prohibited
by applicable law, or except for the sole purpose of extracting data
that You have stored within the Software (including, without
limitation, by means of the Software's built-in export functionality,
or by querying a database instance that You operate). This exception
survives regardless of any other provision of this Agreement.

6. Disclaimer of Warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.

7. Limitation of Liability

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, LICENSOR SHALL NOT BE
LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING OUT OF THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE
SOFTWARE. IF LICENSOR IS FOUND LIABLE NOTWITHSTANDING THE FOREGOING,
LICENSOR'S AGGREGATE LIABILITY SHALL NOT EXCEED THE TOTAL AMOUNT
ACTUALLY PAID BY YOU TO LICENSOR FOR THE SOFTWARE (WHICH, FOR THE
SINGLE-USER EDITION, IS NT$0).

8. No Refunds

The Single-User Edition is provided free of charge and is therefore not
subject to refund.

9. Commitment Upon Discontinuation

In the event Licensor discontinues maintenance or updates of the
Software, instances already deployed by You shall continue to operate.
Your data shall remain within the environment You control, and shall
remain fully exportable via the Software's built-in export
functionality.

10. Governing Law

This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the
laws of the Republic of China (Taiwan).

11. Contact

Inquiries regarding licensing should be directed to support@kakephooa.com.

